{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3116","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3116","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3116\",\"parent_revision\":\"4dd4e833a2209ce3fd00dd802383ba038baa349d9c2a9c787c54f10cb202683f\",\"root_revision\":\"4dd4e833a2209ce3fd00dd802383ba038baa349d9c2a9c787c54f10cb202683f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring the #3060 incident investigation, after a worktree-isolated agent's git worktree vanished mid-task, the Bash tool's working directory kept resetting to that dead worktree's now-nonexistent path on every subsequent Bash call in the session, rather than resetting once or falling back to a live directory.\\n\\nImpact: every following command required an explicit `cd <path> &&` prefix to work around it, repeatedly, not just once after the worktree was lost.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **bash tool working directory sticks to a dead worktree path after a worktree-isolated agent's worktree vanishes** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation - #3060 incident investigation\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"307f385f314fd3f27a95bd936e6d15b08bbebfaaa8ecb909c1eb0e1419c88825\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIoyHw\"}"}